SC IAROM SA Bucuresti is a company having the main activity the research and development in the aerospace area, and it¿s also involved in developing strategies for Romanian Aeronautical Industry, and consulting for the aeronautics and related industry.
Institution experience:
- Complex projects for aeronautics, space and security areas defined by priority directions within R&D programs PNCDI I and II, CEEX;
- Annual reports and strategy for the national aviation industry;
- Studies on Romanian aeronautical industry participation for widening the European capabilities in security and defense;
- Studies and systems for Romanian participation in the GNSS-GALILEO program;
- Research for developing a telemedicine pilot system for saving the person via satellite;
- Studies and research for achieve an airborne system for space topographic data recording and processing.
The company experience - more than 20 years in the R&D activity, achieving 16 complex projects as coordinator within PNCDI I and II and CEEX, of which 6 were completed with working models

ICAS is a public institution of national interest with legal status, under the coordination of Romanian Ministry of Environment and Forests (Law no.46/2008) and under scientific coordination of Agriculture and Forestry Academy of Science (ASAS).
ICAS is the main developer and manager of scientific and technical information in the national forestry sector.
The Mission of ICAS is to give a scientific background to the development and the management of the forestry sector through producing, developing and disseminating scientific and technical information, by setting the national forest inventory, providing professional consulting, generating, transferring and implementing of new and improved technologies, developing innovative products and contributing to the welfare of our society.
At the national level ICAS has been certified by the National Authority for Scientific Research (ANCS) as a component institution of the National Research-Development System and as a Centre of Excellence in Silvobiology and Forest Management.
ICAS is also, certified as an empowered institution for:
- elaborating environmental impact assessment studies;
- environmental reports, for forest management planning, watershed planning, forest road planning;
 - economic and technical studies concerning ecological reconstruction;
 - cadastral and photogrammetric works;
 - preserving and testing the quality of forest seeds;
- testing pesticides in order to be homologated in the forestry field. 
The Quality Management System is in compliance with the ISO 9001 standard.

At the international level ICAS is a full member or collaborator of prestigious international organisations such as: 
- EARSeL ( European Association of Remote Sensing Laboratories);
- IUFRO (International Union of Forest Research Organization);
- EFI (European Forest Institute),;
- ICP-Forests ( National Focal Centre) ;
- IL(S)TER (International Long Term Social and Ecological Research), LTER-Europe;
 - Bioversity International;
- ISTA (International Seed Association);
- FTP (Forest ¿Based Sector Technology Platform) etc. 
- an efficient and active partner for forest-related topics within large international projects in the frame of programmes LIFE+, FP 6, FP7, COST.

